'' vendor/miniaudio -- miniaudio 0.11.26, David Reid's audio library in C (public domain or MIT-0:
'' LICENSE), with stb_vorbis 1.25 as its Ogg Vorbis decoder, as one import:
''
''     #import "vendor/miniaudio" link dynamic        (or 'link static', or neither)
''
'' Every routine, type and constant of miniaudio.h is then callable as miniaudio documents it
'' (https://miniaud.io/docs), unqualified. Playback, capture and duplex devices on WASAPI,
'' DirectSound, WinMM, ALSA, PulseAudio, JACK and CoreAudio, all loaded at run time; decoders for
'' WAV, FLAC, MP3 and Ogg Vorbis; the high-level engine (ma_engine, ma_sound: mixing, groups,
'' fades, spatialisation, streaming) and the low-level pieces under it (ma_device, ma_decoder,
'' ma_encoder, ma_data_converter, ma_resampler, ma_pcm_rb, ma_waveform, ma_noise, the node graph).
''
''     dim as ma_engine engine
''     if ma_engine_init( nullptr, @engine ) <> MA_SUCCESS then print "no audio device" : end 1
''     ma_engine_play_sound( @engine, "chime.ogg", nullptr )
''     sleep 2000, 1                     ' ', 1': a plain 'sleep' ends at a key press
''     ma_engine_uninit( @engine )
''
'' The header is miniaudio.ti, translated by 'tiko c2t' from the header src/prepare.py makes of
'' miniaudio.h (its declarations, with its atomics, pthread types and one unnamed struct written
'' so c2t can take them, every layout unchanged: prepare.py says how it was checked); its banner
'' names that header and its SHA-256. miniaudio-residue.ti holds by hand what the translation
'' could not carry: three static inline helpers and MA_SIZE_MAX. MA_VERSION_STRING is the routine
'' ma_version_string( ): tiko's names are case-blind, so the macro cannot be both.
''
'' THINGS TO KNOW:
'' - The caller allocates miniaudio's objects -- 'dim as ma_engine engine', then ma_engine_init
''   on its address -- and must keep them where they are until uninit: miniaudio's own threads
''   hold pointers into them. Never copy an initialised ma_engine, ma_sound or ma_device.
'' - A data callback (ma_device_config.dataCallback, a custom ma_data_source) is a 'cdecl' proc
''   with the C signature, and RUNS ON MINIAUDIO'S AUDIO THREAD: touch only its arguments and
''   memory set aside before the device started -- no strings, no allocation, no printing.
'' - Frame counts are unsigned (ma_uint32, ma_uint64): 'for i = 0 to n - 1' with n = 0 runs to
''   the type's maximum. Count from 1, or test n first.
'' - The examples in examples/miniaudio: 01-play (the engine), 02-tone (a device and a callback),
''   03-record (capture to a WAV file), 04-decode (files to PCM, no device).
''
'' THE LIBRARY: with 'link static' miniaudio is linked into the program; with 'link dynamic' --
'' and when no '#import' says, which is this package's default -- the shared library, which tiko
'' copies beside the program: miniaudio.dll, miniaudio_linux_x86_64.so on Linux,
'' miniaudio_linux_arm64.so on arm64 Linux, or miniaudio_macos_arm64.dylib on macOS. It needs no
'' system libraries: every audio backend is loaded when a device is opened.
''
'' TARGETS: windows-x86_64 and linux-x86_64 are translated, built and run (RFC-0005 P1). The
'' header stops with #error on every other target until P3 measures its pthread sizes
'' (src/prepare.py); Android's static archives are built, not yet linked or run.
#module "miniaudio"

public #include once "miniaudio.ti"
public #include once "miniaudio-residue.ti"

'' ANDROID IS STATIC ALWAYS: vendorfetch builds only the archive there, as for cJSON.
#if defined( TIKO_LINK_STATIC ) or defined( TIKO_OS_ANDROID )
    #ifdef TIKO_OS_MACOS
        #foreignlib MINIAUDIO static "lib/miniaudio", "framework:CoreFoundation", _
            "framework:CoreAudio", "framework:AudioToolbox"
    #else
        #foreignlib MINIAUDIO static "lib/miniaudio"
    #endif
#else
    #foreignlib MINIAUDIO dynamic "lib/miniaudio"
#endif
